<title>FRANCE: Total sees profitability on the rise.</title>
<headline>Total sees profitability on the rise.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French energy group Total expects a substantial rise in profitability even if oil prices fall back to $16 per barrel, chairman Thierry Desmarest said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The trend is for a substantial improvement in results even in a context of relatively low oil prices,&quot; he told a news conference to announce the group's first-half results.</p>
<p>Brent crude was trading at $23.30 after the United States launched a second missile attack on Iraq.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
